---
/**
 * /nations/bc — every First Nation in British Columbia.
 */
import Record from '../../../layouts/Record.astro';
import BcDirectory from '../../../components/BcDirectory.svelte';
import { getBcNations, DIRECTORY_META, groupByPeople } from '../../../lib/bc-nations';

const nations = getBcNations();
const peoples = groupByPeople();
const tracked = nations.filter((n) => n.records.length || n.mentions.length).length;
const withoutCouncil = nations.filter((n) => !n.tribalCouncil).length;

const forBrowser = nations.map((n) => ({
  name: n.name,
  slug: n.slug,
  people: n.people,
  tribalCouncil: n.tribalCouncil,
  bandNumber: n.bandNumber,
  tracked: n.records.length + n.mentions.length,
}));
---

<Record
  title="First Nations of British Columbia"
  description="A directory of every First Nation headquartered in British Columbia, drawn from the federal band registry, with whatever the record tracks about each."
  kicker="The Nations"
  heading="First Nations of British Columbia"
  standfirst={`${nations.length} Nations, listed from the federal band registry, each with whatever this site has tracked about them.`}
  dateline={`Registry retrieved ${DIRECTORY_META.retrieved}`}
  measure="full"
>
  <div
    class="not-prose grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-px bg-rule border border-rule rounded overflow-hidden mb-12"
  >
    <div class="bg-paper px-5 py-5">
      <p class="font-record text-3xl text-ink leading-none mb-1.5">{nations.length}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-snug">Nations listed</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper px-5 py-5">
      <p class="font-record text-3xl text-ink leading-none mb-1.5">{peoples.length}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-snug">Peoples and Nations represented</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper px-5 py-5">
      <p class="font-record text-3xl text-cedar leading-none mb-1.5">{tracked}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-snug">with something tracked this year</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-paper px-5 py-5">
      <p class="font-record text-3xl text-ink leading-none mb-1.5">
        {nations.length - tracked}
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted leading-snug">with nothing tracked yet</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2>Why 201 and not 203</h2>
    <p>
      You will usually see 203 First Nations quoted for British Columbia, and Indigenous
      Services Canada's own BC Region contains 204 bands. This list holds {nations.length},
      because it is filtered to bands whose administrative office is actually in the
      province — the BC Region also administers a few whose offices sit outside it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Three numbers, three slightly different questions. None of them is wrong. This one is
      stated rather than smoothed over because a directory that quietly picks a number is
      the kind of thing you cannot check.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2>What is here, and what is not</h2>
    <p>
      Names, band numbers and office locations come from the federal band registry. People
      or Nation and Tribal Council affiliation are matched in from a secondary source where
      the match was confident.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tribal Council is blank for {withoutCouncil} of them. <strong>Blank means no confident
      match was found, not that the Nation is unaffiliated.</strong> Those are different
      claims and only one of them is supported here.
    </p>
    <p>
      "Nothing tracked yet" means exactly that — this site has not recorded anything about
      that Nation this year. It is a statement about the coverage of this record, not about
      the Nation.
    </p>
    <p>
      One structural limit is worth naming. This is a registry of <em>bands</em>, and a
      Nation is not always a band. Where a Nation is made up of several communities that
      each appear here separately, anything recorded at the Nation level will not attach to
      the individual community pages — the Nisga'a Villages are the clearest example. That
      is deliberate. A Nation and its communities are related, not interchangeable, and
      quietly merging them would put one community's name against another's affairs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The directory</h2>
    <BcDirectory client:load nations={forBrowser} />
  </section>
</Record>
